    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48-a3">

                <pb facs="0111" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg77"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>The Duke de Gramont to Mr. W. Hoffman.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 18, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I have received the letter which you did me the honor to write to me, of
                    yesterday’s date, in which you say you have been instructed by the cabinet at
                    Washington to take under your protection the subjects of the North German
                    Confederation residing in France. The government of his Majesty has no objection
                    to your charging yourself with this mission, and I hasten to respond to your
                    desire that we give to you our entire assent. * * * * * * *</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GRAMONT.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wickham Hoffman,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Charge d’Affaires, &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
